※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4645

※ A generic function is checked where it is written, with nothing known of a
※ type parameter but what the requirements say: an operator applied to a value
※ of one has to be named by a `pre` clause.  So the message is about the
※ definition, before any call -- and a call is told in the signature what its
※ types must support, rather than finding out from an instantiation.

fn largest(a: T', b: T') → T':
    a ⌈ b

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
